# C19 (spec 2.4). Sign in with auth.http first: the HTTP client keeps the access cookie.
# Saving needs transformations@convert; downloading your own needs transformations@download;
# another user's needs transformations@download_any (admin).
@itemId = <id-from-X-Transformation-Id-or-history>
@targetUserId = <another-user-id>

### Convert and save: 200 immediately, X-Save-Status: pending (the file is written in the background)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/convert
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="targetFormat"

json
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="save"

true
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="people.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

name,city
Ada,Zurich
--b--

### Without save (or save=false): X-Save-Status: not_requested, nothing is kept
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/convert
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="targetFormat"

json
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="people.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

name,city
Ada,Zurich
--b--

### save must be true or false: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/convert
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="targetFormat"

json
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="save"

yes
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="people.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

name,city
Ada,Zurich
--b--

### The save status in history: storageStatus pending → available, hasStoredFile, fileExpiresAt (never the key)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/transformations/history?limit=5

### Download your saved result: 200 attachment; 409 file_not_ready while pending; 404 if unsaved, failed, expired or not yours
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/transformations/history/{{itemId}}/download

### Download someone's saved result (admin): 200; 403 without download_any; 404 for an unknown user or item
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{targetUserId}}/transformations/history/{{itemId}}/download
